{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== e6bd CLAIMED, COMMITTED, AND THE STACK IS PUSHED. Plus: the staleness saga had ONE cause. ===\n\nPUSHED: git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main -> 5 new changes\n  1119 172e: verifier paths resolve the standard class\n  1120 cb6f: add REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE with deep layering\n  1121 cc33: consume per-class fallback chains\n  1122 7f86: ADR 0056 — decompose PydanticAIRunner.run()\n  1123 e6bd: extract interpret_failure from run()      <- TOP, the one that must be green\non top of pushed change 1104 (a574). Commit d09784c6b, trailer verified\n(`verify-commit-ticket: OK`), Change-Id Iaf5858c9..., signed off as RebarBotNava\n<joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>.\n\nEXPECT 1121 AND 1122 TO GO Verified -1 ON THE HEADROOM GUARD, AND THAT IS FINE. cc33 puts\nrunner.py at 782, so cc33's own patchset and the ADR commit on top of it both fail\ntest_structured_run_seam.py's <700 assertion. Verified is cast PER PATCHSET, so an\nintermediate commit cannot be green here — only 1123 (e6bd, 699) restores it. This is exactly\nthe case the operator's standing rule covers: ignore a Verified -1 on an ANCESTOR when it is\nonly the size guard, keep the TOP clean, operator overrides the ancestors manually. Do NOT\n\"fix\" 1121/1122 by relaxing the guard or by squashing.\n\n=== THE ROOT CAUSE OF EVERY FALSE STALENESS READING THIS SESSION (I was wrong twice first) ===\n\n`--ref HEAD` DOES NOT GOVERN THE CLAIM-GATE FRESHNESS RE-CHECK. Only the REBAR_GATE_REF\nENVIRONMENT VARIABLE does. Proven in a single command, both ways, on the same ticket:\n\n    rebar review-plan e6bd --status --ref HEAD                    -> stale-code\n    REBAR_GATE_REF=HEAD rebar review-plan e6bd --status --ref HEAD -> certified\n\nMECHANISM: compute_validity() (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:698) re-hashes each scoped\ndependency file at _hash_basis(..., at_current_gate_ref=True), which resolves\ngate_source.default_ref() — and that DEFAULTS TO origin/main (confirmed:\ngate_source.default_source -> \"attested\", default_ref -> \"origin/main\"). This branch carries\nunpushed commits, and cc33 alone adds ~97 lines to runner.py, so runner.py and\nstructured_run.py genuinely differ from origin/main. Any attestation SCOPED to those files\ntherefore reports a FALSE stale-code unless the env var overrides the ref.\n\nTWO WRONG DIAGNOSES I PUBLISHED BEFORE GETTING THERE — both now retracted, and the earlier\nsession-log entry stating them should be read with this correction:\n  1. \"The review was run against a dirty tree, so it was born stale.\" WRONG. In attested mode\n     the signing basis is the attested SNAPSHOT (current_code_root), not the checkout, so a\n     dirty worktree does not affect signing at all.\n  2. \"Run plan reviews against a clean worktree.\" WRONG and now retracted from the cron\n     prompt. The evidence was in front of me the whole time: I stashed and un-stashed and the\n     verdict did not move — which should have told me the worktree was never the variable.\nI also burned a stash/pop cycle and one whole re-review chasing this. The lesson worth keeping\nis procedural: when a state change you predicted does NOT change the output, that is a\nfalsified hypothesis, not a puzzle to route around.\n\nFOUR STALENESS MODES, all seen live this session, all different triggers:\n  stale-code       a SCOPED dependency file differs from the GATE REF (see above)\n  stale-material   this ticket's own description/AC/file_impact/children changed.\n                   `set-file-impact` COUNTS — I destroyed e6bd's and a49e's good attestations\n                   by setting file_impact to clear a plan-review ADVISORY.\n  stale-pin-drift  a CHILD's plan was edited after the PARENT's review pinned it. 7f86 hit\n                   this because I edited e6bd's and 8229's descriptions after reviewing it.\n  stale-head       an UNSCOPED attestation (no file_impact -> no deps) dies on EVERY commit.\n                   7761 is in this state right now.\nCOMMENTS ARE NOT MATERIAL. Session-log and ticket comments are always safe mid-gate.\n\n=== e6bd, AS LANDED IN THE COMMIT ===\n\nrunner.py 782 -> 699 (clears <700 on THIS patchset), structured_run.py 256 -> 373.\nFull suite 8237 passed / 74 skipped / 0 FAILED. lint 0, typecheck 0.\nHeld-out TDD: I wrote 15 tests, confirmed RED, gave the implementer ONLY 3 happy-path tests,\nand validated the other 12 (arm ordering, metadata, end-to-end) after. Three mutations —\ndisable the sampling translation, drop the budget arm, drop the typed arm — each turned\nheld-out tests red, so the ordering assertions have teeth rather than being tautologies.\n\nA CORRECTION TO e6bd's OWN CERTIFIED PLAN, recorded because the plan text is now wrong:\nthe plan told the implementer to retarget test_llm_failure_matrix.py's CURRENT(<file>:<line>)\nmarkers \"WITHOUT a line number\" so they cannot rot again. THAT IS WRONG. Those markers are\nVALIDATED by test_every_matrix_case_pins_a_current_source_seam, which asserts the anchor has\n`:` followed by digits — and its docstring says the brittleness is deliberate, \"so a later\nstory flipping a row is forced to update the cited seam\". I found this only because I ran the\ntest after making the change. Corrected in the commit: 19 markers retargeted to real anchors\nstructured_run.py:84 (LLMRunnerError step-budget arm), :95 (typed LLMError passthrough), :131\n(broad LLMUnavailableError construction). TWO were deliberately left pointing at runner.py\nbecause they are NOT this ticket's seams and a blanket replace would have swapped a stale-but-\nhonest number for a confidently WRONG symbol: runner.py:502 (per-call req.config may only\nRAISE the operator floor — the usage-limits region 8229 extracts) and runner.py:579\n(valid-JSON wrong-schema exhausting the bounded output retry). Both are stale; both belong to\ntheir own tickets.\n\nNEXT: wait for votes on 1123 (top). Then close 172e/cb6f/cc33 as their changes go Verified +1.\nThen 8229 — its review FAST-FAILS while blocked, so it can only be reviewed AFTER e6bd closes.\nThen a49e (stale-material; also blocked by 8229). Remember REBAR_GATE_REF=HEAD on every gate."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785520660856855001,"uuid":"0618ee62-24ca-49f2-b441-52a8a4dfc484"}